{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
"O, [G]where are you [Am]going?" "To [D]Scarborough fair,"
[G]Savoury [C]sage, rose[Em]mary, and [D]thyme;
"Re[G]member [Am]me to a [D]lass who lives there,
For [C]once she [D7]was a [G]true love of mine.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
"And [G]tell her to [Am]make me a [D]cambric shirt,
[G]Savoury [C]sage, rose[Em]mary, and [D]thyme,
With[G]out any [Am]seam or [D]needlework,
And [C]then she [D7]shall be a [G]true love of mine.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}
"And [G]tell her to [Am]wash it in [D]yonder dry well,
[G]Savoury [C]sage, rose[Em]mary, and [D]thyme,
Where [G]no water [Am]sprung, nor a [D]drop of rain fell,
And [C]then she [D7]shall be a [G]true love of mine.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 4"}
"Tell [G]her to dry it [Am]on yonder [D]thorn,
[G]Savoury [C]sage, rose[Em]mary, and [D]thyme,
Which [G]never bore [Am]blossom since [D]Adam was born,
And [C]then she [D7]shall be a [G]true love of thine."
{end_of_verse}
{x_end: G}
